  "verdict": "The (-2,3,7) pretzel's one-dimensional level-2 state integral, read as a U(1) theory with chirals of charge (1,1,2) at CS level 2, reproduces the triangulation 3D index on every cell m in -2..2, e in -6..6 to q^3 (dictionary fixed on 4_1 and 5_2, half-meridian shifts from Part 12a, one longitude framing integer per knot), and GZ's printed total index to q^7. Closing the contour factorises it into SIX holomorphic blocks in GGM eq (19) form: two unit blocks B_U(x), B_U(1/x) and four doubled blocks B_{sigma,eps}, with the SAME sign and parity on the q and q^{-1} sides; the fusion equals the index at every m to q^7. This is the level-2 fusion rule qou-x3iv Parts 12b-17 were missing. H_Ad at block level: the unit blocks depend on the meridian x = m^2 only; the doubled blocks depend on sigma*(m + 1/m), the FUNDAMENTAL character, whose square is s(x) + 1. sigma-even combinations lie in Z[s(x)], sigma-odd ones do not, and the sigma-grading is tied to the half-integer q powers -- the same ring verdict as the operator route (qou-lzzi), now from explicit blocks.",
